# Arabic range "to" boundary -- the term / upper limit of a bounded interval,
# correlative of "from" (من) in "من ... إلى ...".
# "إلى" (ilā): W. Wright, *A Grammar of the Arabic Language*, 3rd ed., vol. II,
#   §46 -- إلى marks the end point / limit reached ("إلى يوم الأحد"), correlative
#   of من.  Badawi, Carter & Gully, *Modern Written Arabic*, §2.9.
# "الى": the same preposition written without the hamza, a ubiquitous
#   orthographic variant (mirrors marker_until.voc, which lists both forms).
إلى
الى
